<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27376" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lympha</span></b> , ae, f.
		
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύμφη</span>
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>water;</i> esp. clear river or spring water (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lymphae puteales,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					6, 1178</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fluviali spargere lympha,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 4, 635</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2, 459</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulnera lymphis abluere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 13, 531</span></i>
			.— Also, <i>the water</i> in dropsical
			persons: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lympha intercus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ser. Samm. 27, 501</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Personified: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lympha</span></b> .
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A rural deity, the goddess of water</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 1, 6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Lymphae, i. q. Nymphae, <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 1,
				5, 97</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
		1639</span></i>.</div>
